00:38:04,361 --> 00:38:14,360
One of the most dangerous events Dwight may face during a storage tank fire is the possibility of a boil over.

465
00:38:14,361 --> 00:38:25,360
During a torrential storm, the weight of rain water can sometimes cause a floating roof to fail, exposing the oil inside.

466
00:38:25,361 --> 00:38:30,160
A boil over may occur when a crude oil storage tank burns out of control for hours.

467
00:38:31,200 --> 00:38:34,480
The boiling oil on top creates a hot thermal wave,

468
00:38:34,880 --> 00:38:38,600
which sinks and reaches a layer of water near the bottom of the tank,

469
00:38:39,520 --> 00:38:41,340
essentially causing a steam explosion.

470
00:38:43,020 --> 00:38:50,980
So rather than the fuel burning inside the walls of the tank on the surface of the fluid,

471
00:38:50,981 --> 00:38:59,640
it will cause that to basically erupt and expel or eject all of the fuel that's in there all over everything

472
00:38:59,641 --> 00:39:06,080
and then generally involves many more because there are lots and lots of storage tanks near each other.

473
00:39:07,540 --> 00:39:11,760
The objective is to put the fire out before a boil over occurs.

474
00:39:13,240 --> 00:39:18,140
To do that, Williams Fire has developed a host of tools and techniques.

475
00:39:18,141 --> 00:39:26,920
the best protective clothing that you can buy this distance we like to kill fires long distance

476
00:39:26,921 --> 00:39:28,920
we like to do it with the artillery

477
00:39:28,921 --> 00:39:38,680
these are william's big guns trailer mounted water cannons or monitors capable of delivering

478
00:39:38,681 --> 00:39:40,880
up to 6 000 gallons of water per minute

479
00:39:40,881 --> 00:39:52,240
The nozzle and monitor package itself is on a quick action package where we can move it

480
00:39:52,241 --> 00:39:59,600
vertically with just one person and it'll go 360 degrees around.

481
00:39:59,601 --> 00:40:06,200
We mix foam here at the nozzle with the water, make a foam solution delivered as a finished

482
00:40:06,201 --> 00:40:07,200
foam.

483
00:40:07,201 --> 00:40:12,160
to flow 1,000 through 6,000 gallons per minute, and it's portable.

484
00:40:13,360 --> 00:40:17,840
The foam concentrate contains a detergent like hydrocarbon surfactant.

485
00:40:19,300 --> 00:40:24,080
When it lands, it actually runs across the surface of the flammable liquid fire.

486
00:40:24,520 --> 00:40:28,400
It blankets that flammable liquid fire to the point where it suppresses vapor

487
00:40:28,401 --> 00:40:31,900
and occludes the oxygen, so we don't get that vapor-air mixture

488
00:40:31,901 --> 00:40:33,780
and have a continuance of burning.

489
00:40:33,781 --> 00:40:40,720
Once we eliminate the oxygen from the surface of that fire and suppress the vapors, the fire goes out.

490
00:40:43,300 --> 00:40:50,580
Besides foam, Williams Fire also uses a dry chemical called PKW for the final punch.

491
00:40:53,920 --> 00:40:59,280
The dry chemical temporarily interrupts the chain reaction of the combustion process of a fire.

492
00:40:59,281 --> 00:41:06,280
It has a purple dye, so firefighters can easily see it in the stream of water.

493
00:41:06,281 --> 00:41:13,380
This is PKW, the dry chemical of choice for Williams Fire and Hazard Control.

494
00:41:13,381 --> 00:41:20,960
We use it whenever we need a chemical to eliminate a pressure fire.

495
00:41:20,961 --> 00:41:24,120
This is a very fine powder.

496
00:41:24,121 --> 00:41:29,720
introduced through our hydrochem nozzle into our foam stream to eliminate that chemical chain reaction.

497
00:41:32,940 --> 00:41:37,220
Firefighters shoot both foam and dry chemical through the high-pressure water cannons.

498
00:41:38,360 --> 00:41:40,980
But killing many fires requires hand-to-hand combat.

499
00:41:42,480 --> 00:41:47,620
If this is their heavy artillery, then this is their bayonet.

500
00:41:47,621 --> 00:41:59,700
The water foam solution comes in here and it goes out here around this little pipe.

501
00:41:59,701 --> 00:42:03,120
The valve for it is marked water foam.

502
00:42:03,121 --> 00:42:07,500
And you open it first and you start knocking the fire down.

503
00:42:07,501 --> 00:42:12,320
Once the fire gets knocked down, you visualize exactly where your pressure fires are.

504
00:42:12,321 --> 00:42:15,360
you get ready to shoot them out, you simply pop them and shoot them out.

