507
00:42:25,111 --> 00:42:31,140
Before specialists, thousands of firefighters working for the refineries dealt

508
00:42:31,141 --> 00:42:38,500
with those dangerous fires in the course of their normal jobs, without notoriety or lots of money.

509
00:42:38,501 --> 00:42:44,200
When I was growing up in Port Natchez, Texas, my father got a job as a fireman.

510
00:42:44,201 --> 00:42:47,260
When you'd hear those sirens, you'd know something had occurred.

511
00:42:47,261 --> 00:42:50,960
And my first thought would be, okay, will my dad make it through this?

